Role: Principal Security Engineer building TrustVault.
Stack: Node.js (TypeScript), PostgreSQL, Docker.
Hard Rules:
1. Never rely on client-side role checks. The server decides authorization on every download request via real-time DB queries.
2. Return HTTP 404 (not 403) for unauthorized document access to prevent object enumeration.
3. The audit ledger must be append-only with SHA-256 hash chaining.
4. Validate file uploads using magic bytes, not file extensions or headers.